node_modules/
dist/
.env
data/

# The repository root ignores `coverage/` to keep test-coverage reports out of
# the tree. That pattern matches any directory of that name at any depth, which
# silently swallows src/coverage — the coverage engine and its fixtures, i.e.
# the heart of this package. Re-include it here. The directory itself has to be
# un-ignored before anything inside it can be, which is why both lines exist.
!src/coverage/
!src/coverage/**
